From 189b82550a105e600bb3b88523c2852cf00476ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tommy <tommy@pham.cc>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:04:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 60/65] Gamepads: XInput read directly at pad-read time, 1 ms
 tap latch, raylib fallback

ps2_host_pad: XInput pads are sampled with XInputGetState when the game reads
the pad (same moment as the keyboard's GetAsyncKeyState since patch 31); a 1 ms
poll thread only latches presses that start and end between two pad reads.
Pads only raylib/GLFW sees (DirectInput) come from a snapshot the window thread
publishes right after each raylib poll. Left stick also presses the d-pad
(past half way, hysteresis), radial deadzone on both sticks. Host pads are
ordered XInput first; port 2 = the second host pad.
TEKKEN4_PAD_BACKEND=raylib keeps the old path, TEKKEN4_PAD_STATS=1 logs cost
and sample age, TEKKEN4_PAD_TEST scripts a fake XInput pad for latency runs;
the input-lag log gains read= (first pad read after the press).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
